= Using mkosi

== Requirements

- mkosi v26
- ~30GB free space


== Usage

=== Building

Due to a bug in npm < 10 (https://github.com/npm/cli/issues/5998), `mkosi` needs to be run as root.

- Be in the git checkout (gateway)
- `mkosi -C mkosi/ genkey`
  - This only needs to be run once
- Become root (`sudo su -` or `su -`)
- `mkosi -C mkosi/ build`
  - If there are build artifacts from previous runs, append `--force`
  - To include packages and set up for testing in a VM, append `--profile vm`


=== Running

==== Create a QCOW2 image

`mkosi` creates a minimally sized image for installation on target devices, so for a VM we need to expand the image size so that `systemd-repart` can run and do it's work.

For this example the image is `webthings-gateway_2.0.0.26047_x86-64`;

- `qemu-img convert -f raw -O qcow2 ./mkosi/mkosi.output/webthings-gateway_2.0.0.26047_x86-64.raw ./mkosi/mkosi.output/webthings-gateway_2.0.0.26047_x86-64.qcow2 -p`
- `qemu-img resize ./mkosi/mkosi.output/webthings-gateway_2.0.0.26047_x86-64.qcow2 +10G`

This QCOW2 image can then be used by Virtual Machine Manager/libvirt.
